  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 248 PM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nDry and cool conditions will persist throughout the weekend as the \nlarge area of surface high pressure slowly descends southeastward \nacross the Central Plains. Overnight lows Saturday will be even \ncooler given clear skies and light winds, which will lead to very \nefficient radiational cooling, with values in the upper teens \nnorthwest and in the low 20s across the remainder of the forecast \narea. Warming through the day will not be very significant, with \nhighs generally in the low to mid 40s. While still cool, slight \nwarming will occur into Sunday with highs in the mid to upper 40s as \nthe low level flow pattern shifts more southwesterly. PoP mentions \nover southwest Iowa in previous forecasts have been removed for \nSunday/Monday as the shortwave of concern is much further south in \nrecent model runs given the influence of the stronger ridging \nfurther north. The gradual warming trend continues through the early \nparts of the next work week as ridging aloft moves over the Central \nUS, bringing with it warmer air.",
